  "repeat_unit": "{[][$]CC(c1ccccc1)[$],[$]CCCC[$][]}",
  "smiles_depiction": "*CC(c1ccccc1)*.*CCCC*",
  "notation_note": "SEBS is a segmented A-B-A triblock, not a random or alternating copolymer: the two brackets above show the two segment compositions and their approximate ratio, but the real chain is one long hydrogenated-polybutadiene midblock (segment y) flanked by a polystyrene block (segment x) at each end. That block sequence, not the monomer ratio, is why SEBS behaves as a rubber at room temperature yet melts and flows like a thermoplastic. The midblock also contains butylene branches from 1,2-addition alongside the tetramethylene run shown.",
